      "arabic_text": "وَبِهَذَا الْإِسْنَادِ عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ أَحْمَدَ عَنْ أَبِي الْعَلَاءِ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ع قَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And with this chain of narration, from Muhammad ibn Ahmad, from Abu al-Ala', from Abu Abdillah (peace be upon him) who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "إِنَّ الْمُؤْمِنَ مَنْ يَخَافُهُ كُلُّ شَيْءٍ وَذَلِكَ أَنَّهُ عَزِيزٌ فِي دِينِ اللَّهِ وَلَا يَخَافُ مِنْ شَيْءٍ وَهُوَ عَلَامَةُ كُلِّ مُؤْمِنٍ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "The true believer is feared by everything, for he is powerful in the religion of Allah and he does not fear anything. This is the distinctive feature of the believers."
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith describes the spiritual state of the true believer (al-mu'min), characterizing him as one who is feared by all things due to his inner strength and power in the religion of Allah. Because he is not afraid of anything, he becomes a source of awe for creation, marking him as a distinct sign of true faith.",
